Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage for the task  

• "SeriesInstanceUID": filter the exact MR series; join to associated segmentation rows.  
• "Modality": identify the imaging / SEG modality of every SOP instance.  
• "SOPInstanceUID": count unique SOP instances.  
• "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID": find every SEG object that references the chosen MR series.  
• "StudyInstanceUID": (optional) verify we stay inside the same study when exploring data.  

Typical conditions that might be used  

• In "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA":  
  ‑ WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'  
  ‑ WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" IN ( … list of SEG series discovered … )  
  ‑ WHERE "Modality" ILIKE '%MR%' OR "Modality" = 'SEG'  

• In "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS":  
  ‑ WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from very simple inspection to the final aggregation needed for the answer.  Adjust the literal UID or add / remove filters as required.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at the MR series row in DICOM_METADATA
SELECT *
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) List distinct modalities inside that exact MR series (usually just 'MR')
SELECT DISTINCT "Modality"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Count how many SOP instances belong to the MR series
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT "SOPInstanceUID") AS "mr_sop_count"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Find SEG objects that reference the MR series
SELECT *
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) List the SeriesInstanceUIDs of those SEG series (deduplicated)
SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesInstanceUID" AS "seg_series_uid"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Check modality values for the discovered SEG series in DICOM_METADATA
SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesInstanceUID", "Modality"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" IN (
    SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesInstanceUID"
    FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
    WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Count SOP instances for each SEG series
SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "SOPInstanceUID") AS "seg_sop_count"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" IN (
    SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesInstanceUID"
    FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
    WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
)
GROUP BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
ORDER BY "seg_sop_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Union the MR series and all SEG series, tagging each row with modality
SELECT "Modality", "SOPInstanceUID"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'

UNION ALL

SELECT "Modality", "SOPInstanceUID"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" IN (
    SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesInstanceUID"
    FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
    WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Aggregate the union by modality to see which has more SOPs
SELECT "Modality",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "SOPInstanceUID") AS "total_sops"
FROM (
    SELECT "Modality", "SOPInstanceUID"
    FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
    WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'

    UNION ALL

    SELECT "Modality", "SOPInstanceUID"
    FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
    WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesInstanceUID"
        FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
        WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
    )
)
GROUP BY "Modality"
ORDER BY "total_sops" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Same as #9 but restricting to the top‑1 modality with the greatest SOP count
SELECT "Modality",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "SOPInstanceUID") AS "total_sops"
FROM (
    SELECT "Modality", "SOPInstanceUID"
    FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
    WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'

    UNION ALL

    SELECT "Modality", "SOPInstanceUID"
    FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_METADATA"
    WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesInstanceUID"
        FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
        WHERE "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" = '1.3.6.1.4.1.14519.5.2.1.3671.4754.105976129314091491952445656147'
    )
)
GROUP BY "Modality"
ORDER BY "total_sops" DESC
LIMIT 1;
```
